mechanisms.what:
R2 fresh attempt when the file is still missing (Vacant owns one redo). If the first attempt has ended (any settle) and the requested file still does not exist, Vacant launches the SAME pi once more:
- same binary: process.execPath + process.argv[1], the pattern pi's own subagent example uses;
- the parent's own argv, so the same --provider/--model/flags and the same --extension files, including any turn cap the user or harness passed;
- the same positional request, byte-identical;
- a new --session-dir under Vacant's data folder;
- the same cwd.
Vacant waits for it inside `agent_settled`, so pi exits only after the child ends. Then it records the outcome. The child is a normal root session for Vacant: VACANT_PI_PARENT and VACANT_PI_SELF are stripped, so it runs its own Stop check and R0. It also carries VACANT_REDO={of, max_turns}, so it can never redo again, and its Vacant aborts it at max(T1,6) turns with ctx.abort() at turn_end. That is the same API Harbor uses (harbor pi.py:319-322). This is the 're-draw from the original request' that every past gain had (report:257-260; CONFORM re-draw, RUN:219-221), and not a same-session revision, which is the weakest past lever (report:300).

mechanisms.trigger:
On `agent_settled` after the first attempt, including after R0 and after the existing in-session pushback rounds, only if ALL of these hold:
- ctx.mode is print or json;
- root session;
- VACANT_REDO is unset (this is not a redo child);
- VACANT_DO_RUN is unset and there is no contract;
- the named requested file is missing or whitespace-only;
- no redo yet for this person request;
- the first attempt made ≥1 model turn;
- its last assistant stopReason is not 'error' while settle ran. That combination is a provider/infra error, not an abort, so the redo would hit the same wall; it is recorded as infra;
- no recorded bash step of the first attempt matches an external-effect deny-list (git push, npm/pip publish, curl/wget with -X POST/PUT/DELETE or --data, scp, rsync to a host, ssh), because a second attempt would repeat those effects.
NOT triggered in: TUI/RPC (a person is present; the delivery note says the file is missing instead), sub-agents, vacant do, when the file exists (no voting by default), or when no output is named.

mechanisms.where_in_code:
vacant_network/trace/redo.py `redo()`:
- reuses adapters/run.py `Launch` (RUN:122-127) and `run_agent` (RUN:175-209): own process group, stdin /dev/null, PWD set, timeout kills the group;
- argv edits: replace the value of --session-dir with $VACANT_HOME/trace/projects/<p>/redo/<n>/ and drop --continue, -c, --resume, -r, --session and --fork;
- env = os.environ minus VACANT_PI_PARENT and VACANT_PI_SELF (names at AG:245-246), plus VACANT_REDO;
- wall limit clamp(W1,120,1200) s, where W1 is the first attempt's wall time measured by the JS side; JS TIMEOUT redo = limit+120 s (AG:189), and the JS side sends SIGTERM before SIGKILL so Python can kill the group;
- afterwards it re-checks the path and appends a 'redo' event {trigger:'missing_output', turns_first, wall_first, child_session_dir, rc, timed_out, wall_ms, delivered}.
PI_EXTENSION: `const REDO=JSON.parse(process.env.VACANT_REDO||'null')`, and register a turn_end handler ONLY when REDO is set, returning undefined after counting. capture.py (prompt_source/classify, capture.py:195-215, 297-304): when VACANT_REDO is set, record the child's prompt as source 'vacant redo', a copy of the person's request that does not reset the parent's rounds. evidence.window (EV:210-224) accepts 'vacant redo' as that session's request, as it already does for 'vacant do'. Eval side: count 'redo' events in ops/eval/harbor_vacant.py:48-53 and ops/eval/local/analyze_local.py.

design:redo-first.principle_check:
Zero-config:
- no new command, flag, file or setting;
- R0 and R2 switch on only from observable facts: pi's run mode, whether the settle boundary ran, and whether the path the person named exists;
- contracts stay optional;
- variants differ only by wheel, as run_local.sh:6 requires.

Install-minimal:
- same `pipx install` + `vacant install` (harbor_vacant.py install);
- only the generated vacant.ts text changes;
- the redo uses the pi binary already running (process.execPath + argv[1]); nothing else is installed.

Byte-identical when there is no problem:
- the parent registers no turn_end handler;
- the new agent_start, turn_start and agent_settled handlers return undefined, and runner.js:677-681 ignores undefined;
- when the file exists or none is named, no message is added and no child runs, so every model request is unchanged;
- to be verified by sha256 of the request bodies in the simuser 'correct' scenario and the L-fake scenario (1).

Accountability wording:
- R0's text says only what the record shows and what to do next, with no actor and no responsibility words (KS-1 checked by script);
- R2 and R3 send the person's own request unchanged;
- the delivery note records the trigger, what was redone and what happened, and keeps the footer 'does not say whether the answer is right' (zerostop.py:46).

Declared cost:
- R0 and R2 spend past a harness's turn budget, so C3 against A is 'quality at ×Y requests', not same-budget;
- neither can lower a delivered answer, because both fire only when nothing was delivered.

